    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Projects</h2>
    <p style="max-width: none; margin-bottom: 1.5em;">A small set of
    composable tools for malware analysis. <strong>stng</strong>
    extracts strings from binaries; <strong>cleave</strong> decomposes
    binaries and source into capabilities mapped to ATT&amp;CK and
    MBC; <strong>litmus</strong> runs local AI-based detection against
    that output, with models improved through cyclotron, Atomdrift's
    live training loop.</p>

    <ul class="proj-list">
      <li>
        <span class="proj-name"><a href="/litmus/">litmus</a></span>
        <span class="badge badge-beta">beta</span>
        <div class="proj-desc">ClamAV-style local scanner for AI-based malware detection. Runs open models like azoth against capabilities extracted by cleave.</div>
        <div class="proj-links">
          <a href="/litmus/">Details</a>
          <a href="https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/litmus" target="_blank">Source</a>
